WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.770
[dramatic music]

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:10.477
It's a breathtaking
moment for me.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.445
NARRATOR: In the sands
of the necropolis,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:15.582
Basem has made an
incredible discovery.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.283
BASEM GEHAD: So what
we are looking here

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.819
is one fragment of
a mummy portrait

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:26.693
that is painted with the
wax, the encaustic technique.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.628
NARRATOR: Greek
artists from Alexandria

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.464
traveled South through
Egypt along the Nile.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.837
People commissioned
their portraits

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:41.941
from the artists, who painted
with hot beeswax onto wood.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.915
The lifelike portraits
were unlike anything

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.884
in Egyptian art.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.321
People hung their colorful
portraits in their homes.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:58.391
When they died, the portrait
was put on their face

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.994
before they were
mummified in the hope

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.495
their spirit would
remember what they

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:03.863
looked like in the afterlife.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.699
[dramatic music]

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.935
It's really a masterpiece.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.904
NARRATOR: Despite
the layers of dust,

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:15.008
Basem can clearly make out the
face of the woman it depicts.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.143
BASEM GEHAD: We can
realize all the detail--

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:22.515
the hairs, eyes, nose,
lips, and even the necklace,

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.551
the green necklace from emerald.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:29.522
And the tunic, the Greek tunic,
which is painted in purple.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.292
NARRATOR: It's a beautiful
portrait of a Greek woman who

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.327
lived and died here
at Philadelphia

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:41.000
around the time of Cleopatra
some 2,000 years ago.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.369
Basem thinks tomb
robbers must have broken

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.138
the fragile painting
when they tried

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:48.274
to remove it from the grave.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.410
BASEM GEHAD: When it's
broken into small fragments

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:54.013
or slides, for
them, it's useless.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.715
They could not sold
it to the market.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.318
So most probably, they
left it at the site.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.286
For us, it's a treasure.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:03.990
I can't see any kind
of object that could be

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.693
more beautiful than this face.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.164
NARRATOR: It's a
great discovery,

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:15.568
everything Basem has hoped for.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.470
BASEM GEHAD: The
aim of the mission--

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.472
we can say that
it's accomplished.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:23.710
This single piece makes
our work here worth it.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:28.047
Because it's-- in
itself, it's unique.

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.816
NARRATOR: It's
possible that Cleopatra

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:35.021
too would have been buried with
a lifelike portrait of herself.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:38.324
We know very well
that ancient Egyptians

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:42.295
were very keen in keeping
the picture of the deceased.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:45.331
It seems that the
tradition continued

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.666
during the Ptolemaic Period.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.801
They kept the same
tradition, but they

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:53.339
did it their own way using a
new tradition of paintings.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:56.676
And then they put these
wonderful, amazing, awesome

00:02:56.743 --> 00:03:00.813
portraits on the face and then
they wrapped the whole mummy

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.682
in an Egyptian style.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.918
NARRATOR: Basem's
discovery suggests

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:08.588
that even outside Alexandria,
the Greeks of her reign

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:13.960
followed Cleopatra's example
and embraced Egyptian customs.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.963
And Cleopatra's respect
for the old ways

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.265
won her favor with
the Egyptians,

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:21.701
allowing her to rule
over a prosperous

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:25.538
multicultural empire.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:29.309
[music playing]

